    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Almost the entire codebook is best treated as a flat lexicon: most repeated letters/digits do not appear in meaning-consistent substitution frames, and the opaque-index test blocks segmentations like 10/f or K1U without further contrasts. The only defensible productive paradigm is K4F ~ K4U, where the same initial element recurs in the same frame and the final element contrasts with a corresponding face contrast in meaning. This supports one construction K4 + FACE_LOC with K4 contributing 'the four corners of' and {F,U} contributing the face.",
